<title>SPAIN: Spain's Santander not worried about EMU.</title>
<headline>Spain's Santander not worried about EMU.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-03-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spain's Santander Bank is not concerned about the effects of a single European currency on its business, chairman Emilio Botin said.</p>
<p>Speaking at the annual shareholders meeting at the weekend, Botin said his group would be prepared for the changes a European economic and monetary union would bring.</p>
<p>&quot;We don't feel any distrust or fear before what many feel is the threat of the Euro,&quot; Botin said.</p>
<p>&quot;To the contrary, we are preparing to assimilate these changes and reinforce our competitive advantage.&quot;</p>
<p>((-- Madrid Newsroom +341 585-2160))</p>
